{#- ### Verdict — leads with the concern-level label and the authored verdict,
    then the deterministic tally, the worst-case blockquote, the closing
    sentence, and finally the basis of the assessment (what was modeled and
    how). The verdict comes first because it is the one sentence a reader who
    stops after the first paragraph must get; the basis qualifies it and so
    follows it.

    `bullets_intro` frames the blockquote; when the fragment doesn't carry it,
    a deterministic default is emitted.

    Inputs: data.severity, data.opening, data.bullets_intro (optional),
             data.bullets[{title,body,refs}], data.closing.
             severity_emoji is a filter-injected helper.
             verdict_label (renderer-computed): the concern-level wording for
             data.severity, shared with the overview.
             verified_suffixes[] (renderer-computed, one per bullet): a
             plain-language badge for bullets whose findings anchor a
             fully-viable abuse chain, else ''.
             Finding and design-risk references render as compact evidence links.
             intro_line (renderer-computed, optional): what kind of assessment
             this is and the size of the modeled system.
             method_limits (renderer-computed, unconditional): one sentence on
             the method and any screened or unanalysed components.
-#}
### Verdict

{{ severity_emoji(data.severity) }} **{{ verdict_label }}** — {{ data.opening }}
{% if risk_distribution %}
{{ risk_distribution }}
{% endif %}
<br/>

**{{ data.bullets_intro or ("Residual risks worth reviewing:" if data.severity == "green" else "Security concerns behind this assessment:") }}**

<blockquote style="border-left: 3px solid #dc2626; padding: 16px 20px; margin: 0;">

{% for bullet in data.bullets -%}
- **{{ bullet.title }}** — {{ bullet.body }}{{ verified_suffixes[loop.index0] if verified_suffixes else "" }}
{% endfor %}
</blockquote>

<br/>

{{ data.closing }}
{% if intro_line %}
{{ intro_line }}
{% endif %}
{% if method_limits %}
{{ method_limits }}
{% endif %}
